.SH NAME
md_SECURITY \- 🚨 Security Policy 
.PP

.SH "Supported Versions"
.PP
\fBSystemEx\fP is a hobby project under active development\&. 
.br
 Security‑related issues will be addressed as time permits\&.
.SH "Reporting a Vulnerability"
.PP
If you discover a security vulnerability, please report it privately:

.PP
\fBEmail:\fP ambersophia.schroeck@mail.de 
.br
 \fBMaintainer:\fP Amber‑Sophia Schröck (pronouns: dey/deren/dem/dem)

.PP
Please include:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
A clear description of the issue 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Steps to reproduce 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Potential impact 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Suggested mitigation (if any)
.PP
.SH "Scope"
.PP
Security concerns may include:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Unsafe memory operations 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Interop misuse (Linux/macOS/Windows dynamic loading) 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Random engine misuse (ISAAC, Randx) 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Threading primitives (spinlocks, EventGroup) 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
IO handling (CacheStream, WriteStream)
.PP
.SH "Response Process"
.PP
.IP "1." 4
The maintainer reviews the report\&. 
.br

.IP "2." 4
The issue is reproduced and validated\&. 
.br

.IP "3." 4
A fix is prepared and tested\&. 
.br

.IP "4." 4
A patch release or commit is published\&. 
.br

.IP "5." 4
The reporter is notified\&.
.PP

.PP
Thank you for helping keep \fBSystemEx\fP safe and reliable\&. 
